# Netlify SPA fallback for React Router's BrowserRouter.
#
# Without this, requesting a real path directly -- pressing Ctrl+R on
# /official, or opening a shared link to /announcements/<id> -- makes the
# browser ask Netlify for a file that does not exist in build/, and
# Netlify answers with its own 404 page. React never boots, so the router
# never gets the chance to handle the route.
#
# Status 200 is a rewrite, not a redirect: the address bar keeps the
# original path, which is what the router needs. A 301/302 would send the
# visitor to / and lose the route.
#
# This cannot shadow real assets. Netlify looks for an existing file
# before applying these rules, so /static/js/*, /favicon.ico and
# /manifest.json keep serving themselves; only paths with no matching
# file fall through to index.html.
#
# Netlify only. Vercel ignores this file and already applies SPA fallback
# through its Create React App preset, which is why the bug never
# appeared there.
#
# CRA copies everything in public/ into build/ verbatim, so this ships to
# the publish directory with no build configuration.

/*    /index.html   200
